i915: don't require eDP AUX_ENABLE_CAP for VESA backlight (Pixel Slate fix)

The Google Pixel Slate (nocturne, kabylake/ulx, device 0x591c) eDP panel
sets backlight brightness over the DPCD AUX channel
(DP_EDP_BACKLIGHT_BRIGHTNESS_AUX_SET_CAP set) but enables the backlight
via the PWM pin, NOT over AUX (DP_EDP_BACKLIGHT_AUX_ENABLE_CAP is clear).
Its eDP backlight capability registers read:

    DPCD 0x700: 04 fb ff 00 00
      edp_dpcd[1] (GENERAL_CAP_1) = 0xfb -> AUX_ENABLE_CAP (bit2) CLEAR
      edp_dpcd[2] (ADJUSTMENT_CAP)= 0xff -> BRIGHTNESS_AUX_SET_CAP  SET
      edp_dpcd[3] (GENERAL_CAP_2) = 0x00 -> no luminance control

Kernel <= 6.18 gated intel_dp_aux_supports_vesa_backlight() on
drm_edp_backlight_supported() alone and drove this panel correctly via
AUX brightness-set (PWM-pin enable), max_brightness 65535.

7.x added "&& check_if_vesa_backlight_possible()", which hard-requires
DP_EDP_BACKLIGHT_AUX_ENABLE_CAP. This panel lacks that bit, so the check
fails, i915 refuses the VESA AUX backlight and silently falls back to
native PWM (max 7500) which does not physically drive this panel: sysfs
brightness/actual_brightness update but the screen never changes. The
GNOME slider, logind SetBrightness and raw sysfs writes all "succeed"
with no visible effect, and dmesg is clean.

Restore the 6.18 gate (drm_edp_backlight_supported() only) so panels that
do AUX brightness-set with PWM-pin enable work again. check_if_vesa_backlight_possible()
loses its only caller here, so mark it __maybe_unused to avoid
-Wunused-function.

This is BobZKernel's pixel-slate variant (runs only on the Pixel Slate),
so relaxing the gate unconditionally is safe here. Diagnosed from live
DPCD reads on the actual hardware (drm.debug=0x100 boot). Do NOT apply on
the other variants.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_aux_backlight.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_aux_backlight.c
index 7a6c07f6a..6e887afbe 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_aux_backlight.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp_aux_backlight.c
@@ -610,7 +610,7 @@ static int intel_dp_aux_vesa_setup_backlight(struct intel_connector *connector,
 }
 
 static bool
-check_if_vesa_backlight_possible(struct intel_dp *intel_dp)
+__maybe_unused check_if_vesa_backlight_possible(struct intel_dp *intel_dp)
 {
 	int ret;
 	u8 bit_min, bit_max;
@@ -658,8 +658,7 @@ intel_dp_aux_supports_vesa_backlight(struct intel_connector *connector)
 		return true;
 	}
 
-	if (drm_edp_backlight_supported(intel_dp->edp_dpcd) &&
-	    check_if_vesa_backlight_possible(intel_dp)) {
+	if (drm_edp_backlight_supported(intel_dp->edp_dpcd)) { /* BobZKernel pixel-slate: don't require AUX_ENABLE_CAP */
 		drm_dbg_kms(display->drm,
 			    "[CONNECTOR:%d:%s] AUX Backlight Control Supported!\n",
 			    connector->base.base.id, connector->base.name);
